00072 \par
00073 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00074 {\cf20 // TABLE SIZING}\par
00075 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00076 {\cf20 // (Read carefully because this is subtle but it does make sense!)}\par
00077 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00078 {\cf20 // About 'outer_size':}\par
00079 {\cf20 // Its meaning needs to differ slightly depending on if we are using ScrollX/ScrollY flags.}\par
00080 {\cf20 // Default value is ImVec2(0.0f, 0.0f).}\par
00081 {\cf20 //   X}\par
00082 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.x <= 0.0f  ->  Right-align from window/work-rect right-most edge. With -FLT_MIN or 0.0f will align exactly on right-most edge.}\par
00083 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.x  > 0.0f  ->  Set Fixed width.}\par
00084 {\cf20 //   Y with ScrollX/ScrollY disabled: we output table directly in current window}\par
00085 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  < 0.0f  ->  Bottom-align (but will auto extend, unless _NoHostExtendY is set). Not meaningful if parent window can vertically scroll.}\par
00086 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  = 0.0f  ->  No minimum height (but will auto extend, unless _NoHostExtendY is set)}\par
00087 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  > 0.0f  ->  Set Minimum height (but will auto extend, unless _NoHostExtendY is set)}\par
00088 {\cf20 //   Y with ScrollX/ScrollY enabled: using a child window for scrolling}\par
00089 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  < 0.0f  ->  Bottom-align. Not meaningful if parent window can vertically scroll.}\par
00090 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  = 0.0f  ->  Bottom-align, consistent with BeginChild(). Not recommended unless table is last item in parent window.}\par
00091 {\cf20 //   - outer_size.y  > 0.0f  ->  Set Exact height. Recommended when using Scrolling on any axis.}\par
00092 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00093 {\cf20 // Outer size is also affected by the NoHostExtendX/NoHostExtendY flags.}\par
00094 {\cf20 // Important to note how the two flags have slightly different behaviors!}\par
00095 {\cf20 //   - ImGuiTableFlags_NoHostExtendX -> Make outer width auto-fit to columns (overriding outer_size.x value). Only available when ScrollX/ScrollY are disabled and Stretch columns are not used.}\par
00096 {\cf20 //   - ImGuiTableFlags_NoHostExtendY -> Make outer height stop exactly at outer_size.y (prevent auto-extending table past the limit). Only available when ScrollX/ScrollY is disabled. Data below the limit will be clipped and not visible.}\par
00097 {\cf20 // In theory ImGuiTableFlags_NoHostExtendY could be the default and any non-scrolling tables with outer_size.y != 0.0f would use exact height.}\par
00098 {\cf20 // This would be consistent but perhaps less useful and more confusing (as vertically clipped items are not useful and not easily noticeable).}\par
00099 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00100 {\cf20 // About 'inner_width':}\par
00101 {\cf20 //   With ScrollX disabled:}\par
00102 {\cf20 //   - inner_width          ->  *ignored*}\par
00103 {\cf20 //   With ScrollX enabled:}\par
00104 {\cf20 //   - inner_width  < 0.0f  ->  *illegal* fit in known width (right align from outer_size.x) <-- weird}\par
00105 {\cf20 //   - inner_width  = 0.0f  ->  fit in outer_width: Fixed size columns will take space they need (if avail, otherwise shrink down), Stretch columns becomes Fixed columns.}\par
00106 {\cf20 //   - inner_width  > 0.0f  ->  override scrolling width, generally to be larger than outer_size.x. Fixed column take space they need (if avail, otherwise shrink down), Stretch columns share remaining space!}\par
00107 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00108 {\cf20 // Details:}\par
00109 {\cf20 // - If you want to use Stretch columns with ScrollX, you generally need to specify 'inner_width' otherwise the concept}\par
00110 {\cf20 //   of "available space" doesn't make sense.}\par
00111 {\cf20 // - Even if not really useful, we allow 'inner_width < outer_size.x' for consistency and to facilitate understanding}\par
00112 {\cf20 //   of what the value does.}\par
00113 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00114 \par
00115 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00116 {\cf20 // COLUMNS SIZING POLICIES}\par
00117 {\cf20 // (Reference: ImGuiTableFlags_SizingXXX flags and ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthXXX flags)}\par
00118 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00119 {\cf20 // About overriding column sizing policy and width/weight with TableSetupColumn():}\par
00120 {\cf20 // We use a default parameter of -1 for 'init_width'/'init_weight'.}\par
00121 {\cf20 //   - with ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed,    init_width  <= 0 (default)  --> width is automatic}\par
00122 {\cf20 //   - with ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed,    init_width  >  0 (explicit) --> width is custom}\par
00123 {\cf20 //   - with ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch,  init_weight <= 0 (default)  --> weight is 1.0f}\par
00124 {\cf20 //   - with ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch,  init_weight >  0 (explicit) --> weight is custom}\par
00125 {\cf20 // Widths are specified _without_ CellPadding. If you specify a width of 100.0f, the column will be cover (100.0f + Padding * 2.0f)}\par
00126 {\cf20 // and you can fit a 100.0f wide item in it without clipping and with padding honored.}\par
00127 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00128 {\cf20 // About default sizing policy (if you don't specify a ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthXXXX flag)}\par
00129 {\cf20 //   - with Table policy ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedFit      --> default Column policy is ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed, default Width is equal to contents width}\par
00130 {\cf20 //   - with Table policy ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedSame     --> default Column policy is ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthFixed, default Width is max of all contents width}\par
00131 {\cf20 //   - with Table policy ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame   --> default Column policy is ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch, default Weight is 1.0f}\par
00132 {\cf20 //   - with Table policy ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchWeight --> default Column policy is ImGuiTableColumnFlags_WidthStretch, default Weight is proportional to contents}\par
00133 {\cf20 // Default Width and default Weight can be overridden when calling TableSetupColumn().}\par
00134 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00135 {\cf20 // About mixing Fixed/Auto and Stretch columns together:}\par
00136 {\cf20 //   - the typical use of mixing sizing policies is: any number of LEADING Fixed columns, followed by one or two TRAILING Stretch columns.}\par
00137 {\cf20 //   - using mixed policies with ScrollX does not make much sense, as using Stretch columns with ScrollX does not make much sense in the first place!}\par
00138 {\cf20 //     that is, unless 'inner_width' is passed to BeginTable() to explicitly provide a total width to layout columns in.}\par
00139 {\cf20 //   - when using ImGuiTableFlags_SizingFixedSame with mixed columns, only the Fixed/Auto columns will match their widths to the width of the maximum contents.}\par
00140 {\cf20 //   - when using ImGuiTableFlags_SizingStretchSame with mixed columns, only the Stretch columns will match their weights/widths.}\par
00141 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00142 {\cf20 // About using column width:}\par
00143 {\cf20 // If a column is manually resizable or has a width specified with TableSetupColumn():}\par
00144 {\cf20 //   - you may use GetContentRegionAvail().x to query the width available in a given column.}\par
00145 {\cf20 //   - right-side alignment features such as SetNextItemWidth(-x) or PushItemWidth(-x) will rely on this width.}\par
00146 {\cf20 // If the column is not resizable and has no width specified with TableSetupColumn():}\par
00147 {\cf20 //   - its width will be automatic and be set to the max of items submitted.}\par
00148 {\cf20 //   - therefore you generally cannot have ALL items of the columns use e.g. SetNextItemWidth(-FLT_MIN).}\par
00149 {\cf20 //   - but if the column has one or more items of known/fixed size, this will become the reference width used by SetNextItemWidth(-FLT_MIN).}\par
00150 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00151 \par
00152 \par
00153 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00154 {\cf20 // TABLES CLIPPING/CULLING}\par
00155 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00156 {\cf20 // About clipping/culling of Rows in Tables:}\par
00157 {\cf20 // - For large numbers of rows, it is recommended you use ImGuiListClipper to submit only visible rows.}\par
00158 {\cf20 //   ImGuiListClipper is reliant on the fact that rows are of equal height.}\par
00159 {\cf20 //   See 'Demo->Tables->Vertical Scrolling' or 'Demo->Tables->Advanced' for a demo of using the clipper.}\par
00160 {\cf20 // - Note that auto-resizing columns don't play well with using the clipper.}\par
00161 {\cf20 //   By default a table with _ScrollX but without _Resizable will have column auto-resize.}\par
00162 {\cf20 //   So, if you want to use the clipper, make sure to either enable _Resizable, either setup columns width explicitly with _WidthFixed.}\par
00163 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00164 {\cf20 // About clipping/culling of Columns in Tables:}\par
00165 {\cf20 // - Both TableSetColumnIndex() and TableNextColumn() return true when the column is visible or performing}\par
00166 {\cf20 //   width measurements. Otherwise, you may skip submitting the contents of a cell/column, BUT ONLY if you know}\par
00167 {\cf20 //   it is not going to contribute to row height.}\par
00168 {\cf20 //   In many situations, you may skip submitting contents for every column but one (e.g. the first one).}\par
00169 {\cf20 // - Case A: column is not hidden by user, and at least partially in sight (most common case).}\par
00170 {\cf20 // - Case B: column is clipped / out of sight (because of scrolling or parent ClipRect): TableNextColumn() return false as a hint but we still allow layout output.}\par
00171 {\cf20 // - Case C: column is hidden explicitly by the user (e.g. via the context menu, or _DefaultHide column flag, etc.).}\par
00172 {\cf20 //}\par
00173 {\cf20 //                        [A]         [B]          [C]}\par
00174 {\cf20 //  TableNextColumn():    true        false        false       -> [userland] when TableNextColumn() / TableSetColumnIndex() returns false, user can skip submitting items but only if the column doesn't contribute to row height.}\par
00175 {\cf20 //          SkipItems:    false       false        true        -> [internal] when SkipItems is true, most widgets will early out if submitted, resulting is no layout output.}\par
00176 {\cf20 //           ClipRect:    normal      zero-width   zero-width  -> [internal] when ClipRect is zero, ItemAdd() will return false and most widgets will early out mid-way.}\par
00177 {\cf20 //  ImDrawList output:    normal      dummy        dummy       -> [internal] when using the dummy channel, ImDrawList submissions (if any) will be wasted (because cliprect is zero-width anyway).}\par
00178 {\cf20 //}\par
00179 {\cf20 // - We need to distinguish those cases because non-hidden columns that are clipped outside of scrolling bounds should still contribute their height to the row.}\par
00180 {\cf20 //   However, in the majority of cases, the contribution to row height is the same for all columns, or the tallest cells are known by the programmer.}\par
00181 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
00182 {\cf20 // About clipping/culling of whole Tables:}\par
00183 {\cf20 // - Scrolling tables with a known outer size can be clipped earlier as BeginTable() will return false.}\par
00184 {\cf20 //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
